    {
      "@type": "dcat:Dataset",
      "title": "Continuum of Care (CoC) Housing Inventory Count Reports",
      "description": "Continuum of Care (CoC) Homeless Assistance Programs Housing Inventory Count Reports are a snapshot of a CoC\u2019s housing inventory, available at the national and state level, and for each CoC. The reports are based on the Housing Inventory Count (HIC), an inventory of housing conducted on a single night during the last ten days in January. It reflects the number of beds and units available on the night designated for the count that are dedicated to serve persons who are homeless. The HIC also includes information about unmet need.\nNote: This information has not been independently verified by HUD. Where possible, CoCs are encouraged to use HMIS data to generate the HIC. Since compliance with these standards may vary, the reliability and consistency of the homeless counts may also vary among CoCs. Additionally, a shift in the methodology a CoC uses to count the homeless may cause a change in homeless counts between reporting periods. These reports are available annually starting from 2005.",
      "modified": "2019-12-31",
      "accessLevel": "public",
      "identifier": "HUD166",
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "org:Organization",
        "name": "U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development"
